1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:02,790
Your bank flagged you. The reason?

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,230
Where you were born.

3
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:07,740
Banks are told to score
every customer for risk.

4
00:00:07,990 --> 00:00:10,300
The country on your passport counts.

5
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:13,850
Under US tax rules, even a US birthplace

6
00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:16,640
triggers a review you
have to clear yourself.

7
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:19,730
On a public blockchain it gets worse.

8
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,180
Sell a t-shirt to the wrong customer,

9
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:25,830
and software decides you're
one hop from a flagged wallet.

10
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:27,850
Your account gets closed.

11
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,550
You find out after.

12
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:34,100
As Dr. Daniel Kim put it:
it gets told to you at birth,

13
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:36,430
as an accident of where you were born.

14
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,110
Privacy isn't a crime.

15
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:41,350
It's what cash always gave you.

16
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:44,490
Tari is building it into
programmable money:

17
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:47,590
permissionless, programmable, private.
